---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { repos, claims, LICENSE_NAME, LICENSE_URL, SECURITY_URL, TRADEMARK_URL } from '../data/source';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
---

<Layout title="Source Code — Pear Notes" description="The Pear Notes source code is public under the PolyForm Strict 1.0.0 license, so anyone can read and audit how notes are encrypted, stored, and synced.">
  <div class="dot-grid"></div>
  <Header />

  <section class="legal container">
    <h1>Source code</h1>
    <p class="last-updated">Source available under {LICENSE_NAME}</p>

    <p>
      Pear Notes asks you to trust it with your notes, so its code is public. You can read
      exactly how notes are encrypted and how your devices pair and sync,
      instead of taking our word for it.
    </p>

    <h2>The repositories</h2>
    <ul>
      {repos.map(r => (
        <li><a href={r.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>{r.name}</strong></a> — {r.body}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <h2>Check the claims</h2>
    <p>Each privacy claim on this site, and the file in pear-notes-core that carries it out:</p>
    <ul>
      {claims.map(c => (
        <li>{c.claim}: <a href={c.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>{c.path}</code></a></li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <h2>What the license allows</h2>
    <p>
      The code is licensed under the <a href={LICENSE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{LICENSE_NAME}</a>
      license. It is source available, not open source:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You may</strong> read, study, and audit the code for non-commercial purposes, and write about what you find.</li>
      <li><strong>You may not</strong> modify it, redistribute it, or publish it as an app.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The Pear Notes name, logo, icon, and store artwork are not covered by the code license.
      See the <a href={TRADEMARK_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">trademark policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Reporting a security issue</h2>
    <p>
      If you find a way to read, change, or delete someone's notes without their key, bypass a
      note lock, or break pairing, please report it privately using the repository's
      <strong>Report a vulnerability</strong> button or by email, as
      <a href={SECURITY_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SECURITY.md</a> describes.
      Please don't open a public issue for a vulnerability.
    </p>

    <h2>Contributions</h2>
    <p>
      Pull requests aren't accepted. Bug reports and feature ideas are welcome on the
      <a href={`${base}contact/`}>contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
